[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37270"] :question/problem "Find the eigenvectors of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ given that \n\n$$\nB[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ appears on both sides of the equation. Since this matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), right-multiplying the equation by the inverse gives the following expression for $B:$\n\n$$\nB={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $B$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P:$\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-37625/selection/2af822a418eb9befc66cb23518496023284329470164864f91c9854c2cc5d6da" :answer/id #uuid "00741376-4eeb-58cf-a42c-c862621f7b90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37625/selection/eed85fff1c310132f0359c50f92366bdd4fa19a46b8ed174cc9094aeae2f725d" :answer/id #uuid "39699e75-5337-509f-81fc-8edf04e08698" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37625/selection/bfa610a9099d476affe4ee8706af2dd5100d04c3972d9a9bf8a640c43aea30be" :answer/id #uuid "0d171951-79ba-52c1-834d-3c8a9583174d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37625/selection/7662e8e35c42b251a31dd1a399991d84492cba2071401accf6f8eb36af376970" :answer/id #uuid "9819ff40-49cf-5bf4-b9a0-6a1a026ef323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37625/selection/0dc7dc493c16a18a2be028608621dd84d992e310630cfa9b864afebd9b683a04" :answer/id #uuid "ff814f1f-861a-53df-8eab-c7d7c9933124" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37625/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb1a21af-91d7-592e-8dd1-00a6de64dd10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37625/selection/bfa610a9099d476affe4ee8706af2dd5100d04c3972d9a9bf8a640c43aea30be" :answer-field/choices ["q-37625/selection/2af822a418eb9befc66cb23518496023284329470164864f91c9854c2cc5d6da" "q-37625/selection/eed85fff1c310132f0359c50f92366bdd4fa19a46b8ed174cc9094aeae2f725d" "q-37625/selection/bfa610a9099d476affe4ee8706af2dd5100d04c3972d9a9bf8a640c43aea30be" "q-37625/selection/7662e8e35c42b251a31dd1a399991d84492cba2071401accf6f8eb36af376970" "q-37625/selection/0dc7dc493c16a18a2be028608621dd84d992e310630cfa9b864afebd9b683a04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37625" :question/id #uuid "37a50d07-181f-50e1-b1a0-fc697fe75537" :question/math-academy-id "q-37625" :question/problem "Find ${A}^{69}$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have been given the following diagonalization of $A.$\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSo, since $A=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${A}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{A}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the inverse of the matrix $P.$ We get\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{69} & =P{D}^{69}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{69}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{1}^{69} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (-1)^{69}\\end{aligned}](\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-37625/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "634729e9-7633-52d8-99fa-b00fc9cbe96a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37625"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86693/selection/a3320d4fbb663192e5e9d2eaf92902d3e6d1a6f78a53879db9f1f413cba3fa36" :answer/id #uuid "dfbe4327-d426-51eb-9566-12b46c2f2888" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86693/selection/14d2a122205e864b290497e51166b26ae3fb0c03686b1589e00048c92b9345c5" :answer/id #uuid "659cd68d-f5dd-5b66-ac34-b5466c67131d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86693/selection/153ba743a562a958d27d3608e178b7b737b6adcc3bbd51e5b6f35aacf32da135" :answer/id #uuid "112ef994-5951-503c-b981-b847bee05629" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86693/selection/9ad27accf1a245a19fb394760e92f88aeda4cfa08bd14bdec752c8bd10149046" :answer/id #uuid "e8712716-eb93-5e81-9bb9-a32374876573" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86693/selection/ac08e79ab9880c26c07c424c037549c28af6c4bc8e1d4855a19a8d6c3eff2ae9" :answer/id #uuid "22832ab1-f59c-5ff5-ad21-6a9bbd92a87b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86693/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba40485b-f8f4-5729-9939-f38872ecda36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86693/selection/ac08e79ab9880c26c07c424c037549c28af6c4bc8e1d4855a19a8d6c3eff2ae9" :answer-field/choices ["q-86693/selection/a3320d4fbb663192e5e9d2eaf92902d3e6d1a6f78a53879db9f1f413cba3fa36" "q-86693/selection/14d2a122205e864b290497e51166b26ae3fb0c03686b1589e00048c92b9345c5" "q-86693/selection/153ba743a562a958d27d3608e178b7b737b6adcc3bbd51e5b6f35aacf32da135" "q-86693/selection/9ad27accf1a245a19fb394760e92f88aeda4cfa08bd14bdec752c8bd10149046" "q-86693/selection/ac08e79ab9880c26c07c424c037549c28af6c4bc8e1d4855a19a8d6c3eff2ae9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86693" :question/id #uuid "d7c42c03-63a2-5e8d-a07f-3d0a144353b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-86693" :question/problem "Find the eigenvectors of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ appears on both sides of the equation. Since this matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), left-multiplying the equation by the inverse gives the following expression for $B:$ \n\n$$\nB={{{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $B$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=7$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P.$ Computing $P,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P={[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the corresponding eigenvectors are: \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86693/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "237e9db9-a621-5abe-be24-d11ec63840d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86693"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140131/selection/e50b31351dd19349ca8fbea00b83c5e9f6c416a3e9a9cf3fe220e0dc0c8bd0a5" :answer/id #uuid "1d831391-a764-5275-9da6-af685e997707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}40 & 24 \\\\ -48 & -28\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140131/selection/39a8ea4f604759801a9711a0fdc1a0b94bcdf5697944684903fa2f3aef9c3238" :answer/id #uuid "a82a6427-5f0c-5ad4-b6b6-8c6ad6a1715d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}32 & 24 \\\\ -20 & -44\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140131/selection/3b51d427026c1b309f15e76b169a00df308b2793ed140c6401fe9fee90d89287" :answer/id #uuid "4c7a1cbe-47f8-5f2a-ad67-03c898ce4d42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}36 & 20 \\\\ -44 & -28\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140131/selection/f233c43cf37767f0f35c35e93fb86676bc1989e4fd3a260110cd947d7d80a433" :answer/id #uuid "226c020b-96d7-5b65-92f4-12960d29bdb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}48 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -32\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140131/selection/f9467db488a7711a0d17861738a444687111e1e5e8b57d9c7f425cfd68933347" :answer/id #uuid "189bb149-c13a-5813-9a9c-831eebb31939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}40 & 36 \\\\ -32 & -24\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140131/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e5399a4-d8e2-5590-ae53-e40c8018d40e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140131/selection/e50b31351dd19349ca8fbea00b83c5e9f6c416a3e9a9cf3fe220e0dc0c8bd0a5" :answer-field/choices ["q-140131/selection/e50b31351dd19349ca8fbea00b83c5e9f6c416a3e9a9cf3fe220e0dc0c8bd0a5" "q-140131/selection/39a8ea4f604759801a9711a0fdc1a0b94bcdf5697944684903fa2f3aef9c3238" "q-140131/selection/3b51d427026c1b309f15e76b169a00df308b2793ed140c6401fe9fee90d89287" "q-140131/selection/f233c43cf37767f0f35c35e93fb86676bc1989e4fd3a260110cd947d7d80a433" "q-140131/selection/f9467db488a7711a0d17861738a444687111e1e5e8b57d9c7f425cfd68933347"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140131" :question/id #uuid "8edabc41-ebbe-529c-bd32-126001e5080e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140131" :question/problem "Find ${B}^{120},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[60]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[40]{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have been given the following diagonalization of $B:$\n\n$$\nB={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[60]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[40]{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSince $B=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${B}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{B}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{120} & =P{D}^{120}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[60]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[40]{2}\\end{aligned}]}^{120}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt[60]{2})^{120} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (\\sqrt[40]{2})^{120}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -24 \\\\ 12 & 32\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}40 & 24 \\\\ -48 & -28\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140131/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "634729e9-7633-52d8-99fa-b00fc9cbe96a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140131"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140134/selection/ed0b5